												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Early Access Game</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">Get instant access and start playing; get involved with this game as it develops.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“Benny’s Backrooms already has plenty to explore, survive, and scream about, but we still have a lot we want to improve and expand.<br />
<br />
Early Access lets us develop the game alongside the community, so players like you can tell us what’s working, what isn’t, and what you would like to see polished, changed, or added on the road to v1.0.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“Approximately 12 months, although that may change based on player feedback, development scope, and what the game needs before we feel it’s ready for full release.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“We plan to expand Benny’s Backrooms throughout Early Access with more environments, entities, equipment, objectives, progression features, and other gameplay content.<br />
<br />
We’ll also continue improving multiplayer, balance, performance, and overall polish based on what we learn from players.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“Benny’s Backrooms currently features:<br />
<br />
• Several memorable entities not found anywhere else in the Backrooms<br />
• Three procedurally generated liminal space levels<br />
• Online multiplayer lobbies with proximity VOIP and networked physics<br />
• Exploring, surviving, and extracting resources with your company-issued &quot;T-Vac&quot;<br />
• A variety of other unique equipment, tools, and items to find, use, and upgrade<br />
• Character emotes and cosmetics for expressing yourself — or being extremely unhelpful to your friends<br />
• An in-game feedback system so players can easily help shape future development<br />
<br />
The game is fully playable, but players should expect content, balance, systems, performance, and other aspects of the experience to continue evolving throughout development.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“We may increase the price of Benny’s Backrooms after Early Access to reflect the additional content, features, and polish added during development.<br />
<br />
We haven’t made a final decision yet, and we’ll communicate any planned pricing changes in advance.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“We’ll primarily gather feedback through our Discord server, while also keeping a close eye on Steam Discussions, reviews, surveys, playtests, bug reports, and our in-game feedback system.<br />
<br />
We’ll use that feedback alongside gameplay data and our own development goals to identify bugs, improve balance and usability, prioritize fixes, and evaluate potential new content and features.<br />
<br />
Your feedback will help shape Benny’s Backrooms. We can’t implement every suggestion, but we’ll prioritize the ones we believe will have the biggest positive impact.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
